      <notesStmt>
        <note> This article examines the manuscript tradition of the sermon collection attributed to Jean de Villers, a Cistercian abbot who died in 1336. The author, Thomas Falmagne, analyzes the manuscripts and their relationships, focusing on the Cistercian and Parisian origins of the sermons. The article includes a detailed stemma codicum illustrating the manuscript tradition and discusses the historical context of the sermons' transmission.</note>
      </notesStmt>
